      "side": 1,
      "message": "curious on when will we ever break out from this try-again loop ?",
      "revId": "e94e1681645ac2dad200aca81d7d1c2fc3adf5fe",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7c61167a_0e38b101",
        "filename": "fs/fuse/readdir.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 575,
      "author": {
        "id": 1044551
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-13T21:44:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The use case here is that a user filter might remove entries, and indeed might remove all entries. (Imagine if you only want to show files with certain characteristics - you could imagine a READDIR with all entries that need removed, but there could be entries we want in the next set.) Normally a zero-length return signals the end, so we need to have a flag to say \u0027Yes, there weren\u0027t any, but keep going\u0027. But this has to stop when we\u0027ve iterated the entire lower folder.",
      "parentUuid": "64b884ff_a6b29ba9",
      "revId": "e94e1681645ac2dad200aca81d7d1c2fc3adf5fe",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
